
# Student Management Portal - Product Backlog

## Project Goal
To develop a web application that helps manage
student details, attendance, and academic records.

## Product Backlog

| ID | User Story | Priority | Story Points | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| PB-01 | As a developer, I want to set up the project repository. | High | 2 | Done |
| PB-02 | As a user, I want to view the home page. | High | 3 | To Do |
| PB-03 | As an admin, I want to add student details. | High | 5 | To Do |
| PB-04 | As an admin, I want to view all student records. | High | 3 | To Do |
| PB-05 | As an admin, I want to edit student details. | High | 3 | To Do |
| PB-06 | As an admin, I want to delete student records. | Medium | 3 | To Do |
| PB-07 | As a user, I want to search students by name or ID. | Medium | 3 | To Do |
| PB-08 | As an admin, I want secure login functionality. | Medium | 5 | To Do |
| PB-09 | As a faculty member, I want to record attendance. | Medium | 5 | To Do |
| PB-10 | As an admin, I want to generate student reports. | Low | 5 | To Do |
| PB-11 | As a developer, I want to test and fix application bugs. | High | 3 | To Do |
| PB-12 | As a user, I want project documentation. | Medium | 2 | To Do |

## Priority Explanation
- High: Essential features required first.
- Medium: Important features for later sprints.
- Low: Additional features.

## Definition of Done
- Feature works as expected.
- Inputs are validated.
- Testing is completed.
- Code is committed and pushed to GitHub.
- Documentation is updated.
